A||||11||Dan86gt3.8||For anyone that has ever taken off body pannels!||||5||
Z||000000||Dan86gt3.8||08-07-2000||12:13 AM||||Ok I took off alot of body pannels and ground effects, and the like.  I just snipped off all thoose pop-rivets.  Now I have a delima.... how in the heck do I get them back on????  Can you buy theese pop rivvets?  any input??  What have yall used to replace the rivvets?||||reg||5
Z||000001||EdsB52||08-07-2000||12:45 AM||||Any descent body supply shop will have them. Bring whatever is left of them to compare with.||||reg||1
Z||000002||EdsB52||08-07-2000||12:47 AM||||To elaborate a little more. Body paint and supply store.||||reg||1
Z||000003||86SE||08-07-2000||02:20 AM||||I took mine to a place in Omaha called "Nebraska - Iowa Fastener Co."  just took in the plastic/rubber rivets and they matched em right up....<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||14
Z||000004||My7Fieros||08-07-2000||02:24 AM||||GM still makes most all of the fasteners...I order them all the time, and they're cheap! Sometimes I get bumped around from the Pontiac to the Chevrolet dealerships though, because some of the parts are used on diff. cars and the parts #'s change, blah blah blah...but yes, you can still get them through GM.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000005||Spyder||08-07-2000||11:14 AM||||I have seen some that might work in the specialty fastener section in my local home builders supply. (Lowes) ||||reg||1
Z||000006||ponya||08-07-2000||11:20 AM||||Just got done taking off the left rear quarter panel for repair. Went to my local GM dealer and got all the plastic and aluminum rivets needed. Stay away from ebay, they sell them there also, but wayyyyy to costly.<P>Bob||||reg||6
Z||000007||contra||08-07-2000||07:02 PM||||you're al going to hate me for this probably but when i put lower quarter panel scoops on my fiero, i didn't have the time or patience to go get the right clips etc for my ground effects and panels. I just drilled new holes in everything with lots of screws and then covered them with the covers on the ground effects. The original rivet spots were so badly damaged from a pervious scrape on a speed bump i'm guessing by the previous owner, so i really had no choice either. So far they havent fallen off, and i dont think they ever will...and it's completely unnoticable unless you go under my car or take stuff apart  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Gokart||08-07-2000||07:45 PM||||When I put my rockers panels back on last month after getting them painted I got the smallest toggle bolts at the hardware store and they worked perfectly! Use washers for the bolts that will drop into the recessed area under the covers.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||3
Z||000009||deceler8||08-07-2000||08:21 PM||||For stuff like inner fender liners and rear splash shields, plastic wall anchors can't be beat. They're so much better than what was originally used that it ain't funny.<P>Neat signature, huh ?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=64144&a=464935&p=25703947"> ||||reg||10
Z||000010||Dan86gt3.8||08-08-2000||12:26 AM||||Thanks for all the sugestions.  We have a tab at a local fastners store (realiance) and hopefully they will have them if not then I guess I will have to order it from gm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
